 When importing these for the first time, parsing and denotation of their own source is performed by them being loaded from right there, before the idempotent bundles they produce replace the arbitrarily structured sources. Using Interface directly as we did to access the sum#i function, this logic would apply only to the one module specified, but as in the case of parsing and denotation, modules may in turn import others that don't exist yet either. Getting to specify Interface as a loader module for Node will have it use the resolve#b and load#b commands for all imports: 

loader#script/highlight(` node16 --loader=./Blik_2023_interface.js ./haverbeke_2012_acorn.js;
 node20.2 --import 'data:text/javascript;import("module").then(({register})=>register("./Blik_2023_interface.js",{parentURL:pathToFileURL("./")}));' ./haverbeke_2012_acorn.js;
 node20.7 --import=./Blik_2023_interface.js ./haverbeke_2012_acorn.js;
 node21.1 --import=./Blik_2023_interface.js --experimental-detect-module ./haverbeke_2012_acorn.js;
  # module detection introduced and unflagged in 21.1 and 22.7 
  # fails to detect modules with eg. export statements far in the file, 
  # so a classic package.json entry has been needed to ensure module syntax: 
 cat package.json 2>/dev/null || echo {} | jq '.type="module"' > package.json;
`){display:block;width:90%;margin:0px 5%;border-radius:.5em;border:1px solid #43a047;background:black;overflow:scroll;white-space:pre;font-family:monospace;color:#616161}

 With the "import" flag, module loading happens on a secondary thread where Interface needs to explicitly register#b itself from the primary one. The command line context is also lost there, hence resolve#i suppresses primary imports to let Interface infer#i it directly after registration. A local context identifies the client agent#b ((agent)#script/highlight(`{node,browser,virtual}`){display:inline;word-break:break-all;font-family:inherit}), corresponding language features#b ((features)#script/highlight(`{assertions,attributes,json}`){display:inline;word-break:break-all;font-family:inherit}), thread#b rank, command line flags ((flags)#script/highlight(`[loader,legacy,inspected]`){display:inline;word-break:break-all;font-family:inherit}), locates and loads source definitions ((sources)#b, sourcemap#b), and declares an idempotent peer#b, window#b and scope#b identity for remote fetch#b{}ing and precedent tracking. A non-virtual Node client agency#b then is the condition for the registration procedure, which in turn determines the loader#b thread for the inference command#b to observe#b and delegate#b to (latter can also start threads if supplied a function or module declaration like worker#b). Prompt#b is available for procedures to re-open the command line in case of further context missing. 

