(Claim your own property on the Web.)#h2
{text-align:left;}


 Since requests to a server act as the module loader for browser clients, we can further extend Interface by (opening a port)#b to listen to them. Such a function will need two things: a declaration of the model#b you want to expose, and of the protocol#b you want to use. From a command line, we can supply these as modules specifiers, like "./static.js" and "./protocol.json/host/local". After loading these, the expose#b function uses prompt#b to supply missing contexts (port, certification, encryption keys), then composes them into a server routing requests to responses. 

